  "interpretation": [
    "Outer_T with W<=1 can be treated as a thermally diluted hard spectrum at the given area; this does not prove actual spectral thermalization.",
    "Flux-equivalent Teff has W=1 by construction. It is the coolest single-temperature equilibrium Planck emitter that can carry the specified bolometric flux from that area.",
    "A softer assigned shape with W>1 is an unconstrained non-LTE/spectral-shape sensitivity or needs a changed emitting area, reprocessing history or energy distribution. It is not automatically an attainable thermal photosphere or a credible worst case.",
    "Non-LTE line/continuum emission and mixed-temperature areas can differ from these single-temperature proxies; actual frequency-dependent transfer remains unresolved."
  ]
